[I] A password-based encryption utility

[T] scrypt is a file encryption utility built around the scrypt key
[T] derivation function, which was originally developed for the Tarsnap
[T] backup system and is designed to be far more resistant to hardware
[T] brute-force attacks than PBKDF2 or bcrypt.

[U] https://www.tarsnap.com/scrypt.html

[A] Scrypt Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

